> Can anyone explain what this warning message means

It means your model might not have converged on a good solution, only a "local maximum" (or the algorithm may have simply stopped looking because the gradient didn't point out any obvious place to look next).

> When I investigated “optim.gradient”, below were the elements that had non-zero gradient:
>
>
>
> dv1_t2~~dv1_t1
>
> dv1_t3~~dv1_t1
>
> dv1_t4~~dv1_t1
>
> 0.04
>
> 0.003
>
> -0.002
>
> dv1_t2~~dv1_t3
>
> dv1_t2~~dv1_t4
>
> dv1_t2~~dv1_t2
>
> -0.003
>
> 0.002
>
> -0.016
>
> dv1_t1~~dv1_t1
>
> -0.025
>
>

All these are about your dv* variables.  What does their correlation matrix look like?

Does this continue to occur when you treat self and other as separate outcomes instead of trying to extract a higher-order common factor "latent"?

Terrence D. Jorgensen
Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics
